      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Ivica Safranko",
        "email": "safranko@msn.com",
        "date": "2026-11-11T13:44:59Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(post): grblHAL names a smoothing ask it cannot bound\n\ngrblHAL's core lists G61 only - no G64 P or other tolerance word - so\nwith per-operation smoothing (#616) on, the post now writes one\n\"SMOOTHING NOT WRITTEN - GRBLHAL STATES NO SMOOTHING TOLERANCE\" note\nper program (as Fanuc and Mazak do) instead of dropping the ask\nsilently; the ask resets at each section end. Pinned by\nsmoothing::fanuc_and_mazak_name_the_ask_once_and_write_no_unbounded_word.\nAlso corrects the canned-cycle comment: G85 is listed but never mapped.\n\nRefs #710\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "e0c3c0c89d4cf012a10b278191081714382b2fa5",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/NeoTech/Camcraft/git/trees/e0c3c0c89d4cf012a10b278191081714382b2fa5"
